\ Resource-limit tests for exact gate walking.
\ A full gate interval invokes a complete sauce. To avoid an
\ effectively endless scan toward distant coordinates, each
\ user-level year search has at most 1024 gate-gap calculations.
\ These synthetic checks exhaust the limit BEFORE the sauce call;
\ they do not have to compute hundreds of actual gate intervals.
\ Moving from a blocked gate must not alter its index or position.

To check the exhausted gate work budget:
  Begin bounded gate walking.
  Put 0 into the gate step budget's steps remaining.
  Put 0 into the gate walk's current index.
  Put -15055671 into the gate walk's current position.
  Move to the next positive gate.
  If the gate step budget's exhausted is not 1,
    put "A positive gate move ignored the exhausted gate budget." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current index is not 0,
    put "A blocked positive gate move changed the index." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055671,
    put "A blocked positive gate move changed the day." into the check report; exit.
  Move to the next negative gate.
  If the gate walk's current index is not 0,
    put "A blocked negative gate move changed the index." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055671,
    put "A blocked negative gate move changed the day." into the check report; exit.
  Begin bounded gate walking.
  If the gate step budget's exhausted is not 0,
    put "A fresh gate query inherited exhausted status." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate step budget's steps remaining is not 1024,
    put "A fresh gate query did not restore its bounded allowance." into the check report; exit.


\ These checks commit known canonical gap lengths directly, so they
\ catch broken atomic updates without running the 46-drop sauce.
To check atomic native gate movement:
  Begin bounded gate walking.
  Put 0 into the gate walk's current index.
  Put -15055671 into the gate walk's current position.
  Publish the measured positive gate gap given 1 and 345.
  If the gate walk's current index is not 1,
    put "The measured positive native gap chose the wrong gate." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055326,
    put "The measured positive native gap chose the wrong position." into the check report; exit.
  Publish the measured negative gate gap given 0 and 345.
  If the gate walk's current index is not 0,
    put "The measured backward native gap did not reach zero." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055671,
    put "The measured backward native gap did not return to Foundation." into the check report; exit.
  Publish the measured negative gate gap given -1 and 503.
  If the gate walk's current index is not -1,
    put "The measured negative native gap chose the wrong gate." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15056174,
    put "The measured negative native gap chose the wrong position." into the check report; exit.
  Publish the measured positive gate gap given 0 and 503.
  If the gate walk's current index is not 0,
    put "The measured positive return did not reach gate zero." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055671,
    put "The measured positive return did not reach Foundation." into the check report; exit.
  Publish the measured positive gate gap given 1 and 41.
  If the gate step budget's exhausted is not 1,
    put "A too-short native gate interval did not mark failure." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current index is not 0,
    put "An invalid short native gap changed the gate." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055671,
    put "An invalid short native gap changed the position." into the check report; exit.
  Begin bounded gate walking.
  Publish the measured negative gate gap given -1 and 964.
  If the gate step budget's exhausted is not 1,
    put "A too-long native gate interval did not mark failure." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current index is not 0,
    put "An invalid long native gap changed the gate." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055671,
    put "An invalid long native gap changed the position." into the check report; exit.

\ Reject unreachable native indices immediately, without a sauce call.
To check native gate rejection boundaries:
  Begin bounded gate walking.
  Put 400000000 into the gate walk's current index.
  Put -15055671 into the gate walk's current position.
  Move to the next positive gate.
  If the gate step budget's exhausted is not 1,
    put "An unsupported positive gate index did not fail." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current index is not 400000000,
    put "A failed positive gate move changed its index." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055671,
    put "A failed positive gate move changed its coordinate." into the check report; exit.
  Begin bounded gate walking.
  Put -400000000 into the gate walk's current index.
  Move to the next negative gate.
  If the gate step budget's exhausted is not 1,
    put "An unsupported negative gate index did not fail." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current index is not -400000000,
    put "A failed negative gate move changed its index." into the check report; exit.
  Locate a gate given 1025.
  If the gate step budget's exhausted is not 1,
    put "A distant positive gate locate was not rejected immediately." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current index is not 0,
    put "A rejected positive locate moved the gate." into the check report; exit.
  Locate a gate given -1025.
  If the gate step budget's exhausted is not 1,
    put "A distant negative gate locate was not rejected immediately." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current index is not 0,
    put "A rejected negative locate moved the gate." into the check report; exit.
